Once you know what to worry about, you know when you need to be extra
patient as compared to moderately patient.  Also, if you use some sort of
"detect monsters" spell, amulet of ESP, etc. you know what's coming before
it gets to you, which gives you a few turns to react instead of having a
master mind flayer show up next to you with no warning, and having to
react in a single turn.

I personally play with tiles, which means all of the major demons show up
easily -- I know how to recognize the Juiblex tile instantly, for example.
I think this gives me an advantage over someone who just has a bunch of &
characters around them -- I can easily tell a Hezrou from Orcus from
Dispater from Demogorgon from a Balrog.  Getting those confused could
easily mean death.

With respect to the VotD in particular, if you're careful not to wake up
any monsters (don't step on the squeaky boards) they're fairly easy to
clear out quickly, and without an overwhelming number of messages.

